  "question": {
    "text": "A given object takes $\\mathrm{n}$ times the time to slide down $45^{\\circ}$ rough inclined plane as it takes the time to slide down an identical perfectly smooth $45^{\\circ}$ inclined plane. The coefficient of kinetic friction between the object and the surface of inclined plane is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "PwZ22",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{1-\\frac{1}{n^2}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DsIjx",
      "text": "$1-n^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TKM3H",
      "text": "$1-\\frac{1}{n^2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "UX1Gz",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{1-n^2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/Nmax6sj6xBwhtZz6rdfm1IVRwHLYaGrCtcxZ7IFPJro.original.fullsize.png\"><br />Case-1 : No friction\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{a}=\\mathrm{g} \\sin \\theta \\\\\n& \\ell=\\frac{1}{2}(\\mathrm{~g} \\sin \\theta) \\mathrm{t}_1^2 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{t}_1=\\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\ell}{\\mathrm{g} \\sin \\theta}}\n\\end{aligned}$\nCase-2 : With friction\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{a}=\\mathrm{g} \\sin \\theta-\\mu \\mathrm{g} \\cos \\theta \\\\\n& \\ell=\\frac{1}{2}(\\mathrm{~g} \\sin \\theta-\\mu \\mathrm{g} \\cos \\theta) \\mathrm{t}_2^2 \\\\\n& \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\ell}{\\mathrm{g} \\sin \\theta-\\mu g \\cos \\theta}}=\\mathrm{n} \\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\ell}{\\mathrm{g} \\sin \\theta}} \\\\\n& \\mu=1-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{n}^2}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
